  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target audience for this meme is individuals who may be familiar with or perpetuate ableist stereotypes, particularly those who find humor in infantilizing portrayals of people with developmental disabilities. The meme is designed to appeal to viewers who enjoy simplistic, repetitive, or pitiable depictions of people with Down syndrome, often reinforcing the trope that such individuals are intellectually limited or incapable of complex self-expression. The humor derives from the perceived 'sameness' or lack of individuality implied by the repeated name 'bob,' which targets an audience that may not recognize or challenge the harmful nature of this stereotype.",
